[repo-allocation name=cx-repos
  [doc [#
THE REPO ALLOCATION — every tracked path in this tree, assigned to the
repository it moves to under the approved multi-repo shape (#1589, the owner
approved the shape 2026-09-21; the execution tracker is #1591). This file is
the allocation as DATA; scripts/repos_allocation_gate.cx is the check that
every tracked file lands in exactly one repo and that no rule here is dead.
It is what each extraction's history filter consumes, and it is the #1077
lesson — enumerate every artifact dimension before anything moves — made
executable.

Nothing here carries a `RULED:` id yet: the decision page superseding
cx_partition.md §5/§5.1 is item 5 on #1591. Until it lands this file states
the plan, and the gate keeps the plan total over the tree.

TWO KINDS OF ROW.
  [repo name= group= ring= ships= about= status=? at=? pins=? vmodule=? why=?]
      one row per destination repository. `group` is the front-page group
      (core | platform | binding | ecosystem | dist), `ring` is 0, 1 or none,
      `ships` is how the repo reaches a user (binary | package | pypi | crate |
      go-module | v-module | editor | none | archived).
      `status=extracted` says the extraction is DONE (RULED: RS-12): the
      repository exists, it owns its paths, and none of them is tracked here
      any more -- so the row carries no `[path]` rules, `at=` records the sha
      `cx` pins it at in deps.cxd, and the gate exempts it from the empty-repo
      refusal while adding the converse one (a `status=extracted` repo that is
      still the first match for a tracked file is an extraction stopped half
      way). Absent `status` means the plan is still a plan.
      `pins='<repo> ...'` and `vmodule=<m>` are the V products' import
      graph (RULED: RS-24, owner D28a): `pins` is the Pins column of the
      #1589 table -- the repositories this one builds on, acyclic -- and
      `vmodule` names the V module the repository compiles from `vcx/<m>/`
      (D31a: flat). A product row gains `vmodule` in the commit that splits
      it. xap's split made xap `vcx/xap/` (`module xap`, the composer with
      it); what is left in `vcx/platform/` (`module platform`) is the RESIDUE
      of the products whose own split has not merged, each file allocated by
      its rule below, and the last split empties it. scripts/product_import_gate.cx holds every import under a
      vmodule directory to these pins; the rings (the `core` rows) are always
      importable.
  [path prefix= repo=]  /  [path exact= repo=]
      one allocation rule. A tracked file belongs to the FIRST rule, in
      document order, whose `exact` equals the path or whose `prefix` is a
      leading substring of it. Specific rules are therefore written ABOVE
      general ones; the gate refuses a rule that matches no file, which is how
      a shadowed or stale rule is caught.

HOW TO READ A DECISION HERE. Where a module's repo is not the obvious one,
the rule carries a `why=`. The recurring reasons, once:
  - split by PRODUCT, not by dependency graph (owner, 2026-09-21);
  - the ring membership test (cx_partition.md §10): a module that imports
    nothing and opens no socket is Ring 1 and lives with the language —
    did, vc, authz, bus, the xsp frame codec, iowatch;
  - a shared codec stays in the language repo: saml/scim/oidc/soap/graphql/
    ws/email/http-client have callers outside the one product;
  - a module whose only consumer is one product moves to that product:
    ft → store, sasl → mail, diagram → tooling;
  - the store owns engine, streams (journal/live/audit) AND server, as
    Postgres does; the session module sits above it in identity;
  - `scripts/`, `tools/`, `docs*/`, `bench/`, `examples/`, `_gate_evidence/`
    and the root files are the build, release, site and evidence machinery of
    the whole — they go to `cx`, the distribution repo, and are re-homed per
    repo as each extraction lands (a repo takes its own gates with it).
#]]

  [; ── the destinations ─────────────────────────────────────────────── ]
  [repo name=cx group=dist ring=none ships=binary about='the front door: pins every repo, builds the four cx builds and libcx-core/libcx, holds the site, the release, the installer']
  [repo name=cx-core-data group=core ring=0 ships=binary about='the data format: reader, writer, canonical form, schema, codecs, libcx-core, the data-only cx']
  [repo name=cx-core-code group=core ring=1 ships=binary about='the language: evaluator, stdlib, LSP, libcx, the cli and embed builds']
  [repo name=cx-platform-net group=platform ring=none ships=binary vmodule=cxnet status=extracted at=0a4f2114af1e29a19362b24069061c913c9a0374 pins='cx-core-code' about='sockets, TLS, the HTTP server, the XSP transport bindings, ftp, sftp, file_surface' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, RS-24, #1591 item 20), the third V product (after core-data): its own vcx/cxnet/ (module cxnet) and vcx/transport/ leave with it. It owns no tracked path here any more; cx reaches it through deps.cxd, which pins it at the sha at= records, and registry/modules.cxd\'s http, net, ftp and sftp rows -- plus the file_surface catalog row -- name the pinned checkout']
  [repo name=cx-platform-mail group=platform ring=none ships=binary vmodule=mail pins='cx-platform-net' about='SMTP and IMAP, server and client cores, sasl']
  [repo name=cx-platform-identity group=platform ring=none ships=binary pins='cx-platform-store cx-platform-net' about='sessions, the XSP-AUTH handshake, principal mint, did:web']
  [repo name=cx-platform-store group=platform ring=none ships=binary vmodule=store pins='cx-core-code cx-platform-net' about='the storage engine, its substrates, journal/live/audit, ft, and the store server']
  [repo name=cx-platform-db group=platform ring=none ships=binary vmodule=cxdb pins='cx-core-code' about='external database access: $sql-*, $redis-*, the drivers']
  [repo name=cx-platform-fabric group=platform ring=none ships=binary pins='cx-platform-store cx-platform-identity' about='messaging and fabric-serve']
  [repo name=cx-platform-xap group=platform ring=none ships=binary vmodule=xap pins='cx-platform-net cx-platform-mail cx-platform-identity cx-platform-store cx-platform-db cx-platform-fabric' about='the application host, compose, dist, schema, market, the reference deployments']
  [repo name=cx-platform-flow group=platform ring=none ships=package status=extracted at=78ea045510278dee3b0a522ab7f168e42e020fab about='workflow; its CLI verbs stay in the binary' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, RS-20, #1591 item 15), the second of them. Its [path] rules are retired because it owns no tracked path here any more; `cx` reaches it through deps.cxd, which pins it at the sha `at=` records. What RS-20 kept in `cx` is claimed by rules of its own and not by this row: the `cx flow` verbs (vcx/cmd/flow*.v, repo=cx) and the flow-perform act seam (vcx/platform/coordination.v, repo=cx-platform-xap)']
  [repo name=cx-platform-connector group=platform ring=none ships=package about='the connector kit and sync']
  [repo name=cx-platform-sso group=platform ring=none ships=package status=extracted at=1e814e5aae6327a8218cc3fe69b43a03517e92bf about='enterprise sign-on, the interop lane' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, #1591 item 11), the first of them. It has no [path] rules because it owns no tracked path here any more; `cx` reaches it through deps.cxd, which pins it at the sha `at=` records, and the gate exempts a status=extracted repo from the empty-repo refusal for exactly that reason -- the row is the pin\'s counterpart, not a plan waiting to be executed']
  [repo name=cx-platform-ux group=platform ring=none ships=package status=extracted at=ef9248093389d42f6726042bfc254351445db4bc about='the web and terminal surfaces' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, #1591 item 12), with cx-platform-agent: the x/ graduation. It owns no tracked path here any more; cx reaches it through deps.cxd at the sha at= records, and registry/modules.cxd\'s ux, ux-web and ux-tui rows name the pinned checkout']
  [repo name=cx-platform-agent group=platform ring=none ships=package status=extracted at=b4ab532f4e2cb55f31f3c895c1df501c8dcd9544 about='tools, mcp, mcp-server, a2a, a2a-xap, llm, run, adjudicate' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, #1591 item 12), with cx-platform-ux: the x/ graduation. It owns no tracked path here any more; cx reaches it through deps.cxd at the sha at= records, and registry/modules.cxd\'s eight agent rows name the pinned checkout']
  [repo name=cx-binding-python group=binding ring=none ships=pypi about='cxlib for Python']
  [repo name=cx-binding-go group=binding ring=none ships=go-module about='cxlib for Go']
  [repo name=cx-binding-rust group=binding ring=none ships=crate about='cxlib for Rust']
  [repo name=cx-binding-v group=binding ring=none ships=v-module about='the native reference binding']
  [repo name=cx-binding-typescript group=binding ring=none ships=archived about='archived at the ABI it was frozen with; lang/_archived/README.md names the version']
  [repo name=cx-binding-java group=binding ring=none ships=archived about='archived at the ABI it was frozen with; lang/_archived/README.md names the version']
