  [; ── platform: identity ────────────────────────────────────────────── ]
  [path prefix='vcx/platform/stdlib_session' repo=cx-platform-identity]
  [path prefix='vcx/platform/identity_connector_builtins' repo=cx-platform-identity why='RS-6 (#1589, #1591 item 9): the credential binding, the token store and the secret handle that were the connector kit native half. The store half of the same move needs no rule — vcx/store/store_connector_builtins.v is led to the store by the vcx/store/ prefix, and a second rule for it would be a dead one']
  [path prefix='vcx/platform/stdlib_xsp_auth' repo=cx-platform-identity]
  [path prefix='vcx/code/stdlib_xsp_auth' repo=cx-platform-identity why='the DECLARED Ring-1 half of cx-platform/xsp-auth (modules.cxd half=): the pure XSP-AUTH calculus, which RS-24 moved into vcx/code because the store server runs it and the store V module may not import identity (D34a). A module moves whole (#1609), so the half stays with the module, as the smtp/imap halves do (RS-19); the store\'s calls into it are the RS-24 store branch\'s LETTER']
  [path exact='stdlib/session.cx' repo=cx-platform-identity]
  [path exact='stdlib/xsp-auth.cx' repo=cx-platform-identity why='the handshake calculus became a module of its own (RULED: RS-15); its natives are here too, as its declared Ring-1 half in vcx/code since RS-24']
  [; RS-14's two new surfaces. did-web is #1589's own words — identity holds
     "did:web resolution (the one impure did verb)" — so the module, its page,
     its corpus and its natives land here. vc-revocation is NOT named by
     #1589's per-repo bullets: the journal it appends to is the store's, but
     the PRODUCT is credential lifecycle, and identity is where the credential
     surface lives beside session, the handshake and the principal mint. The
     alternative (cx-platform-store, on the substrate) is a LETTER on this
     branch's RESULTS.md, not a settled reading. ]
